    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d192">

                <pb facs="0345" n="173" xml:id="pg173"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 841.857/401</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Consul at Cork</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Frost</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Cork</hi> (<hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Queenstown</hi>)</placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1917-03-13">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">March 13, 1917</hi></date>. <lb/> [<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Received 11 a.m.</hi>]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Seven lives lost in sinking of Cunarder <hi rendition="#italic">Folia</hi> out of
                    crew of 78. <hi rendition="#italic">Folia</hi> bound New York to Avonmouth.
                    Torpedoed without warning 5 miles off Earn Head, County Water ford, in heavy fog
                    Sunday, 7.20 a.m. Dr. Core and officers reach Bristol this morning. Am
                    telegraphing Consul there; this also to Ambassador, Consul General-</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Frost</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
